# Trigger each function by hand through the local Dapr sidecar (VS Code REST Client or Visual Studio).
# Start the stack first (F5, or the "deps: up" task). The orders API should be running on http://localhost:5080.
@dapr = http://localhost:3500

### EVENT: publish order-placed to the "events" pub/sub component (RabbitMQ locally).
# Use an order id that exists in the orders API; unknown ids are logged and dropped.
POST {{dapr}}/v1.0/publish/events/order-placed
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "0192f0a0-0000-7000-8000-000000000001" }

### FILE (object storage), step 1: put a file into the local object store.
POST {{dapr}}/v1.0/bindings/object-storage
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operation": "create",
  "data": "order_ref,customer_name,sku,quantity,unit_price\nB-3001,Northwind,WIDGET-1,2,25.00\n",
  "metadata": { "fileName": "orders-3001.csv" }
}

### FILE (object storage), step 2: send the "object created" notification (S3 format), as S3 -> SQS would.
POST {{dapr}}/v1.0/bindings/object-created
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "operation": "create",
  "data": {
    "Records": [
      {
        "eventName": "ObjectCreated:Put",
        "s3": { "bucket": { "name": "local" }, "object": { "key": "orders-3001.csv", "size": 70 } }
      }
    ]
  }
}

### FILE (drop folder): no request needed. Copy samples/orders.csv into drop/incoming/.
# It moves to drop/processed/ (or drop/failed/ with an .error.txt for samples/orders-invalid.csv).

### Health and metrics of the worker (F5 port)
GET http://localhost:5100/health

###
GET http://localhost:5100/metrics
